:::

# A *swiper*, wired to `wd.subscribe`

::: swiper-tagline
Darkmown owns the reactive `slide` state, the indicator dots, and the live readout —
declaratively, with no hand-written JavaScript. The things a framework this small
deliberately *doesn't* ship — arrow-key navigation, pointer **drag / swipe**, and the
sliding transition — live in a colocated `index.js` that talks to the very same state
through `window.wd.subscribe` and `window.wd.set`.
:::
:::

::: swiper-stage

<div class="swiper-viewport" data-swiper tabindex="0" role="group" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Project gallery — drag, or use the arrow keys">
<div class="swiper-track" data-swiper-track>
